   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The address pins A1 and A0, with RD and WR, select one of the three ports or the control word register.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "49-51",
       "sha": "b61b44c0210d511282b43858a62f7bcaf65c01a4964c7bc692ae0c0392b3508d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Port A is an 8-bit data output latch/buffer and an 8-bit data input latch; its pins PA3-0 are the lower nibble and PA7-4 the upper.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "42-43",
       "sha": "949da481c31dd9d44b1db049751966acff159b3d7f157fbf51de7b6a6a6b2b2a"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "81-82",
       "sha": "2fff61a5e538bc66a9aad39f0b509debfbbd388b3e44d1b87455a78dbdc1c367"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "With A1 A0 = 0 0, RD low, WR high and CS low, a read puts port A on the data bus.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "52-53",
       "sha": "c81189e382c858ea89101e193af87450b740e7671e508ed7214cf4d0e1c9cb6e"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "104",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "In mode 1 with port A an input, and in mode 2, a read of port A also clears the input buffer full flag, interrupt request and input latch.",
